Hrmph! So yer the Trainers Elesa was
talkin' about, huh.{VAR BE01}
I'm Clay. I'm the Gym Leader 'round
these parts.{VAR BE01}
Don't be expectin' no welcome, now.{VAR BE01}
'Cause when we lowered that bridge,
the Team Plasma guys we'd caught{VAR BE00}
done escaped in all the ruckus!{VAR BE01}

Cheren: What a bother.{VAR BE01}
We're grateful that you lowered the
bridge, but how is it our fault that{VAR BE00}
they escaped?{VAR BE01}

Clay: Ya can say whatever ya want.{VAR BE01}
But what's important is y'all showed up,
and then Team Plasma escaped.{VAR BE01}
Maybe it's a little heavy-handed, but
you oughtta start lookin' for{VAR BE00}
Team Plasma, too.{VAR BE01}
Yer both talented Trainers, aren't ya?{VAR BE01}

Tell ya what...{VAR BE01}
If ya find Team Plasma, I'll let ya
challenge my Gym!{VAR BE01}
Life's all about give and take!{VAR BE01}

Cheren: Well, I suppose that's fair.{VAR BE01}
But really, we would have looked
for Team Plasma even if he hadn't asked.{VAR BE01}
I can get stronger while beating that
bothersome bunch...{VAR BE01}

Ghetsis: Clay.
It's a pleasure to meet you.{VAR BE01}
I am Ghetsis, of Team Plasma.{VAR BE01}
I've come to pick up my associates
who are in your care.{VAR BE01}

Clay: I don't need no thanks, now.{VAR BE01}
Yer buddies were tryin' to steal
some folks' Pokémon.{VAR BE01}

Ghetsis: What's this? It seems as if
there has been some misunderstanding.{VAR BE01}
We only free Pokémon from wicked people.{VAR BE01}

Clay: Well, that sounds real nice,
if it's true.{VAR BE01}
I may not talk purty, but at least
I'm an honest man.{VAR BE01}
You talk real nice, but what yer sayin'
kinda sounds like lyin'.{VAR BE01}
So tell me plain, what are ya tryin'
to say?{VAR BE01}

Ghetsis: Team Plasma also has an interest
in Driftveil City.{VAR BE01}
And we have many, many more members
besides those who are here...{VAR BE01}

Clay: ...Well, I can't tell if yer lyin' or
not, but I reckon you've won this{VAR BE00}
without a fight.{VAR BE01}
Hrrmph. Fine. Take 'em and git!{VAR BE01}

Ghetsis: A decision worthy of a
businessman called the Miner King.{VAR BE01}
Your grasp of the situation
is outstanding.{VAR BE01}
Well then, we will be taking
our colleagues off your hands...{VAR BE01}

Ghetsis: Don't worry, my fellow servant
of the king...{VAR BE01}
We are two of the Seven Sages,
are we not?{VAR BE01}
Well then, everyone, I expect that we
will meet again somewhere.{VAR BE01}

Clay: Sorry to let Team Plasma go after
you tracked 'em down, fellas.{VAR BE01}
Say, why don't we cheer ourselves up
with a Pokémon battle?{VAR BE01}
Don't keep me waitin'!{VAR BE01}

Cheren: Well, we avoided a fight in
the middle of the city, anyway.{VAR BE01}
Still, I can't help but think Ghetsis isn't
just an ordinary person.{VAR BE01}
I'm off to go make my Pokémon stronger.{VAR BE01}
I really don't want to lose
to that Clay guy.{VAR BE01}
Actually, I'm going to win my
Gym Badge in a flawless victory!{VAR BE01}

Our Gym Leader, Clay, is in the
middle of something right now.{VAR BE00}
Please come again later.

Hey, were you at the Gym just now?{VAR BE01}
Oh, hey! That's Driftveil's Gym Badge!
Oh, that's totally cool. That's amazing.{VAR BE01}

No, no, no! I can't get distracted being
all impressed with your shiny new Badge!{VAR BE01}
I'm also a Trainer!
At times like this you battle, right?{VAR BE01}

Bianca: I haven't had a Pokémon battle
with you in a while, {VAR 0100 0000}.{VAR BE01}
You've become totally strong, huh?{VAR BE01}
I'm not that strong, so I don't know
how to say it, but I think you're way{VAR BE00}
tuned in to how your Pokémon feel!{VAR BE01}
Oh, you know what! I want to share this
HM with you, {VAR 0100 0000}!{VAR BE01}

Bianca: My papa gave it to me after
he tried to take me home that time.{VAR BE01}
I'm sure it's so I can come home anytime
he wants, though...{VAR BE01}
Oh, hey, I have to share this with
Cheren, too...{VAR BE01}
See you, {VAR 0100 0000}! Buh-bye!{VAR BE01}

Hey there, Trainer!{VAR BE01}
Have you ever battled the Elite Four
of the Pokémon League?{VAR BE01}
You can't battle them unless you
have eight Gym Badges, right?

Oh, ocean...{VAR BE01}
I wonder if the tears I've cried
will flow all the way to Olivine City.

Those Team Plasma meanies forced me
to battle them.{VAR BE01}
And when I lost, they stole my Pokémon!

The Pokémon of lightning and the Pokémon
of wind are both known to come and go{VAR BE00}
as they please.

On the other side of the ocean, there
are a lot of different people and a lot of{VAR BE00}
different Pokémon, aren't there?

The old guy on Route 6 is searching for
legendary Pokémon.{VAR BE01}
If you're interested, go talk to him!

I'm a heartbreaker...
My name... Charles.{VAR BE01}
I wanted to get the attention of a girl
I like, so I learned a new style of{VAR BE00}
Pokémon battling.{VAR BE01}
Its name... Triple Battle!
Want to learn about it?

In Triple Battles, you send out three
Pokémon at a time and battle!{VAR BE01}
The rules are simple: just make all of
your opponent's Pokémon faint.{VAR BE01}
And that's a rough explanation
of Triple Battles.{VAR BE01}

You've got a good attitude, don't you!{VAR BE01}
I'm a heartbreaker...
My name... Charles.{VAR BE01}
I'm always at full throttle.{VAR BE01}

Sheesh. That's embarrassing. Getting
schooled when I was planning to teach.{VAR BE01}
Still, you have potential!{VAR BE01}
You have to understand your Pokémon
to win in a Triple Battle.{VAR BE01}
If you want more Triple Battles, you
should go to Opelucid City.

